-- Dungeon plans for the run leader (.bot run), exported by turtle-agent (plan-export). Plan format v1; the mapping is
-- docs/play/dungeon-run-leader.md ("From plan v1 to rows"). The plan file in turtle-agent is the single source: edit it
-- there and export again, never these rows by hand. The plan row carries the unit lists cc_priority, cc_always and kill_first
-- (columns from 20261015200000_world.sql). Never edit this file once applied; export a new one.
--
-- Shadowfang Keep (map 33): the whole plan again, 10 legs (rethilgore, razorclaw_the_butcher, baron_silverlaine,
-- commander_springvale, courtyard_door, odo_the_blindwatcher_yard, odo_the_blindwatcher, fenrus_the_devourer,
-- wolf_master_nandos, archmage_arugal; status 'draft (not mapped, not live-checked)'), exported with the options of the
-- newest sfk migration's header (20261024050100_world.sql):
--   turtle-agent plan-export --mmaps <map 33 mmaps> --allow-draft --gm-cross-direct --approach-hops \
--     --rev bed9fae --stamp 20261024154000 --out <dir> shadowfang_keep
-- This migration supersedes 20261024153300_world.sql (it stays as applied and is not edited). Data fix from the
-- r36 slotI run of 2026-10-24 (RUN-LESSONS.md): the walk back replayed step 1, whose move point at -232.68 2111.82
-- stands 11.2 yd from Deathstalker Adamant (3849, the friendly prisoner in the entrance cells at -243.7 2113.7 whose
-- gossip opens the courtyard door at step 130/131); the run leader read him as a hop unit (within kHopPullYd 15 yd of
-- the point), pulled him, and the tank engaged and killed him; step 130 then failed with 'gossip 3849 option 1 cannot
-- be done: none alive within 40 yd, a dead one lies nearby (respawns in 4 h 36 min)'.
--   * The plan JSON needed no row change: no pull/boss/hold row and no cc_priority/cc_always/kill_first list of any
--     plan in the repo lists 3849, 3850 or any other entry one of its own gossip/open steps names (the new pin test
--     test_no_plan_pulls_an_event_unit checks every migration; the only overlap anywhere is Zul'Farrak's Bly hold,
--     which fights Sergeant Bly 7604 by design after his gossip wakes the event, so holds are out of the pin). The
--     re-export of the unchanged plan (turtle-agent bed9fae, map 33 mmaps, same options) is byte-identical to
--     20261024153300_world.sql in every step/leg/plan row (318 steps); only the plan row's source rev, the stamp and
--     this header differ.
--   * The guard is in the module, not the rows: ai::PlanNamesEventUnit (DungeonPlanPolicy.h) reports an entry that any
--     gossip/open/use_on/use_item/ritual step of the plan names; the glue (BotCommands.cpp) leaves such a unit out of
--     the move step's hopUnits, and PickPull (DungeonRunPolicy.h) never picks one for a hop (a move's or the walk
--     back's replay). A pull/boss/hold step's own units are unaffected. Pinned by TestHopNeverPullsAnEventUnit in
--     tools/test_dungeon_run_policy.cpp (move step skips 3849, still pulls the ordinary unit beside him, the walk
--     back's replay skips him too, entry-gated picks still take him).
--   * NEEDS THE MODULE CHANGE (as 20261024153300 and 20261024050100): load this migration only on a build that contains
--     TortoiseBots fix/wait-object-gone (kPlanFlagGoneIsDone accepted on a wait_object row, DungeonRunPolicy.h
--     WaitObjectGoneIsDone) and the hop event-unit guard above. A module without the gone flag refuses flag 256 on a
--     wait_object row (BadParam) and skips that row, so the plan it loads has fewer steps than the plan row announces,
--     which the run client refuses.
--   * not in the rows (as 20261024153300): the Alliance gossip with Ashcrombe 3850 (the schema has no team-specific
--     step form), Arugal's Lair 18971 (opens by itself when Nandos dies) and the config entry
--     AiPlayerbot.BotGossipNpcs += 3849 (3850 for an Alliance party), which the module needs for the Adamant gossip
--     at all.
-- Plan check (turtle-agent plan-check --from-leg 7, map 33 mmaps, 2026-10-24, turtle-agent bed9fae): ok, 40 points, the
-- same 4 detour warnings and 4 run-leader-hop notices as the plan of d1f521a minus the fixed boss hop (no failures);
-- carried over from 20261024153300_world.sql (the rows are identical, no new check needed).
-- The boss section at the end (ai_dungeon_boss, the pattern of 20261021114931_world.sql) is added by hand: the
-- exporter does not write that table. The eight map-33 bosses are unchanged from 20261024153300_world.sql.

-- Idempotent: each plan's rows are deleted, then inserted. The tables come from 20261014150000_world.sql.
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_step` WHERE `plan` = 'shadowfang_keep';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_leg` WHERE `plan` = 'shadowfang_keep';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_plan` WHERE `plan` = 'shadowfang_keep';

DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_boss` WHERE `map` IN (33);
